          coreTension: "The word 'kachah' is in the inauguration passage, so it can only make mandatory the things explicitly listed in that same passage. But many inauguration requirements - like the details of priestly garments - are written in other Torah sections. 'Kachah' cannot reach those.",
          coreMove: "The daf ends without answering. This is an open stub - 'milta' - signaling the discussion continues on the next page. The question is deliberately left dangling to invite the learner to ask: what verse would extend the principle?",
