          ahaMoment: "The raw-meat scene is vivid: a worshipper brings an animal, the priest's servant demands raw meat, the worshipper protests, the servant says 'give it now or I take it by force.' This is Temple service turned extortion - a shocking portrait of institutional corruption.",
          learningBlocker: "Students may think the 'delay of bird-offerings' means the priests refused to accept the offerings at all. In fact, they accepted them - but processed them slowly, keeping the women waiting for days.",
          memoryAnchor: "Two Eli-sons sins: delay the kanim (bird-offerings) - women stuck waiting, kept from husbands, scripture calls it immorality. Take raw meat before fat burned - intimidation and extortion of worshippers. Both: priests serving themselves, not God."
