          shortSummary: "The Gemara brings three proofs that Persia will ultimately defeat Rome, based on the lineage established above. However, Rav dissents: Persia will fall to Rome because the Persians destroy synagogues. The disagreement turns on whether geopolitical prophecy or moral conduct determines the outcome. The passage also touches on when Mashiach can be expected to come - not until Rome has ruled the whole world for nine months, based on a verse from Micah.",
          whats: "This is one of the Gemara's most explicit eschatological passages. The debate between the majority view (Persia defeats Rome) and Rav (Rome defeats Persia) reflects two different frameworks for how history unfolds: one based on prophetic lineage, the other based on moral accountability for destroying sacred spaces.",
