          coreTension: "Mezuza marks a domestic residence, not a sacred site. The Temple Mount is sacred (kodesh) not residential (dirat adam). These are different halakhic categories: domestic sanctity vs. Temple sanctity. The mezuza belongs in the first category, not the second.",
          coreMove: "The Gemara identifies three distinct reasons for exemption (not-dwelling, not-honor, not-mundane-residential), showing that mezuza obligation is multi-conditional: a space must be (1) used as a dwelling, (2) used with dignity, and (3) not a sacred precinct reserved for Temple service.",
          resolution: "The three-part framework is established. The Temple Mount/chamber exemption definitively answers the question of the Parhedrin chamber: since the whole Temple is categorically exempt, the Parhedrin chamber's mezuza must be rabbinic only. This confirms the Sages' position against Rav Yehuda.",
