            vilna_line: 29, en: "The Gemara then asks: <b>Rather, why do I</b> need the emphasis of the verse: <b>Your house,</b> if every house is obligated in the mitzva of <i>mezuza</i>? The Gemara answers: This could be understood <b>in accordance with</b> the opinion <b>of Rava, as Rava said:</b> Your house is interpreted to mean that the <i>mezuza</i> is placed in <b>the way that you enter</b> the house. <b>And when a person lifts</b> his foot to begin walking, <b>he lifts his right foot first.</b> Therefore, the <i>mezuza</i> is affixed on the right side of the doorway.", en_lit: "Rather, why do I Your house, in accordance with of Rava, as Rava said: the way that you enter And when a person lifts he lifts his right foot first.",
