          whats: "A dispute about the common priest's belt: does it match the KG's regular-year belt (kilayim, wool-linen mix) or the KG's Yom Kippur belt (buz, pure linen)? Rav Dimi reports the sages of Eretz Yisrael disagree without identifying who holds each position. Ravin clarifies: Rabbi says the common priest's belt is kilayim; Rabbi Elazar b'Rabbi Shimon says linen. A baraita about the phrase 'al besaro yilbash' (he shall wear on his flesh) from the trum hadeshen passage shows that the mitzna and avnet are full priestly garments requiring all four items, resolving who said what.",
