          coreMove: "The Gemara runs the actual cubit count: Heikhal 100 cubits from the north wall, an 11-cubit gap, the 32-cubit altar, the 16-cubit ramp, and 22 cubits to the south wall. Laid end to end, the numbers leave the altar's center well south of the courtyard's midpoint, so a perfectly centered altar is not geometrically possible.",
          resolution: "Middot's own measurements rule out R. Yehuda's centered-altar view, confirming that Middot follows R. Eliezer ben Yaakov, whose offset-to-the-south placement matches the cubit count.",
