            vilna_line: 6, en: "The Gemara questions the assertion that one <i>tanna</i> envisions the chambers as one coming via the left. <b>But didn't the Master say: All turns that you turn should be only to the right,</b> which in certain cases is <b>to the east?</b> Here the turns are to the left. The Gemara answers: <b>This</b> restriction <b>applies only in</b> the course of performing <b>the</b> Temple <b>service; however, here, it is a mere reckoning,</b> and no priest actually proceeded that way from one chamber to the other.", en_lit: "But didn’t the Master say: All turns that you turn should be only to the right, to the east? This applies only in the service; however, here, it is a mere reckoning,",
