          title: "Five trigger foods: when an emission is oness and when it is not",
          whats: "The specific foods that cause seminal emission are listed and discussed. Five foods are identified: fine flour, eggs, wine, garlic, and others. The Gemara then raises a related question: what is the legal status of a kohen who has a seminal emission during the preparation period - is it attributed to illness (oness) or to his own eating? The distinction matters because an unavoidable emission (oness) might not disqualify him.",
