          whats: "The Gemara derives midnight as the cutoff between burning and ash removal from two competing Leviticus verses: 'all night he shall burn it' vs. 'all night... he shall remove the ashes.' Since both claim 'all night,' Rav divides the night in half. Rav Kahana then raises an objection from our own mishna (resolved on 20b).",
