          ahaMoment: "The same word gever carries both meanings in Hebrew. This linguistic ambiguity embedded in the mishna is exactly the kind of thing the Gemara loves to unpack, it is not sloppy language but intentional use of a term that needs clarification.",
          learningBlocker: "Learners expect the Gemara to declare a winner once baraitot are cited, missing that here the baraitot support opposite sides and the dispute is left standing, with the narrative interlude about Rav and R. Sheila's manners carrying as much weight as the textual argument itself.",
          memoryAnchor: "Gever = man or rooster? Rav says man (the Temple crier); R. Sheila says rooster. Rav as guest disseminator: challenged, defended by precedent, declined to stand down."
