          whats: "King Agrippa was so impressed by Gevini's voice that he sent him gifts; yet the voice of the KG announcing purification to the mikveh was heard in Jericho (ten parasangs). Other Temple sounds also reached Jericho. R. Levi explains why sounds carry farther at night: the sun's sphere produces a constant roar all day; at night the sun passes through the celestial roof and the roar continues upward, leaving the lower world quieter. Rome's din and the sun's noise cancel each other.",
