          coreMove: "Abaye locates the answer in the ketoret's unique proximity: unlike animal offerings burned on the outer altar, incense is offered in the most intimate possible nearness to the divine presence. Rava extends the logic with an analogy - a young Torah scholar who issues rulings draws on that same kind of closeness, which is why he too prospers materially. The first-timer-only rule follows naturally: since the privilege is so great, demand from first-timers never runs dry, so no priest ever needs a second turn.",
