          coreMove: "The Gemara clarifies that the incident occurred during the rest of the year, not on Yom Kippur, and the father of Rabbi Avin then states the underlying principle directly: a daily offering slaughtered before dawn is invalid, because the daytime requirement for slaughter is absolute and admits no after-the-fact exception.",
