          memoryAnchor: "5 immersions x 2 sanctifications = 10 sanctifications. Each garment change requires: sanctify, undress, immerse, dress, sanctify.",
          learnerQuestion: "Why does the High Priest immerse five times and sanctify his hands and feet ten times over the course of Yom Kippur?",
          coreTension: "The Mishna asserts specific numbers - five immersions, ten sanctifications - without yet explaining why; the Gemara must establish both the geometry of where these immersions happened (the chamber above the Water Gate) and, in the sugyot that follow, the textual basis for the numbers themselves.",
          coreMove: "The Gemara opens its explanation with an architectural detail: the immersion chamber stood above the twenty-cubit Water Gate, making the chamber itself at least twenty-three cubits above ground - a feature it needs to account for in describing the High Priest's movement through the Temple precincts.",
