          coreMove: "Abaye answers on two tracks depending on whose view is followed - Reish Lakish's ein ma'avirin principle locks the order in one way, while R. Yochanan's view that the verse teaches the incense's own timing supports it differently - and the sugya continues building the rest of the sequence (two lamps, incense, limbs, meal-offering, libation) on the same kind of textual anchoring.",
