          learnerQuestion: "The Mishna says the bull stands between the vestibule and the altar - but is that universally agreed?",
          coreTension: "The Mishna's stated location for the bull (between the vestibule and altar) needs an author, since the Rabbis are known to hold a different position.",
          coreMove: "The Gemara identifies R. Yehuda as the source of the Mishna's ruling, linking the confession's location to where the bull's blood is later sprinkled - the Rabbis place the confession further east in the Azarah.",
          takeaway: {
            type: "legal_principle",
            text: "The Mishna's seemingly neutral description of the bull's location actually follows one specific tanna, R. Yehuda, whose view ties the confession site to the blood-sprinkling site."
          },
