        lines: [
          { id: "yoma-036b-l34", kind: "gemara", he: "תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן:\n״וְכִפֶּר״, בְּכַפָּרַת דְּבָרִים הַכָּתוּב מְדַבֵּר. אַתָּה\nאוֹמֵר בְּכַפָּרַת דְּבָרִים, אוֹ אֵינוֹ אֶלָּא כַּפָּרַת\nדָּמִים.",
            vilna_line: 34, en: "§ <b>The Sages taught</b> in a halakhic midrash that it is written: “And Aaron is to offer his own bull as a sin-offering <b>and atone</b> for himself and for his household” (Leviticus 16:6). Apparently, <b>the verse is speaking of atonement</b> achieved through <b>words</b> of confession. Do <b>you say</b> it is <b>atonement</b> achieved through <b>words, or perhaps it is only atonement</b> achieved through sprinkling <b>blood,</b> as each mention of atonement associated with an offering involves the sprinkling of blood on the altar?", en_lit: "The Sages taught and atone the verse is speaking of atonement words you say atonement words, or perhaps it is only atonement blood,",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.36b.10", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-036b-l37", kind: "gemara", he: "הֲרֵי אֲנִי דָּן: נֶאֶמְרָה כָּאן ״כַּפָּרָה״, וְנֶאֶמְרָה\nלְהַלָּן ״כַּפָּרָה״. מָה ״כַּפָּרָה״ הָאֲמוּרָה בַּשָּׂעִיר\n— דְּבָרִים, אַף ״כַּפָּרָה״ הָאֲמוּרָה בַּפָּר — דְּבָרִים.",
            vilna_line: 37, en: "<b>I will infer</b> via a verbal analogy: <b>Atonement is stated here,</b> with regard to the bull of the sin-offering, <b>and atonement is stated there,</b> with regard to the scapegoat: “And the goat designated by the lottery for Azazel shall be left standing alive before God, to atone with it” (Leviticus 16:10). <b>Just as</b> the <b>atonement that is stated with regard to the goat</b> is atonement achieved through <b>words,</b> as neither is the goat slaughtered nor is its blood sprinkled on the altar, <b>so too,</b> the <b>atonement stated with regard to the bull</b> refers to atonement achieved through <b>words.</b>", en_lit: "I will infer Atonement is stated here, and atonement is stated there, Just as atonement that is stated with regard to the goat words, so too, atonement stated with regard to the bull words.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.36b.11", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-036b-l40", kind: "gemara", he: "וְאִם נַפְשְׁךָ לוֹמַר: הֲרֵי הוּא אוֹמֵר ״וְהִקְרִיב\nאַהֲרֹן אֶת פַּר הַחַטָּאת אֲשֶׁר לוֹ וְכִפֶּר\nבַּעֲדוֹ וּבְעַד בֵּיתוֹ״, וַעֲדַיִין לֹא נִשְׁחַט הַפָּר.",
            vilna_line: 40, en: "<b>And if it is your wish to state</b> a claim rejecting that proof, there is a different proof. <b>It says: “And Aaron shall then offer his bull of sin-offering and atone for himself and his household.</b> And he shall slaughter his bull of sin-offering” (Leviticus 16:11). Here, the term atonement is used despite the fact that <b>the bull has not yet been slaughtered.</b> Apparently, the atonement of the bull is achieved through confession and not through sprinkling the blood.", en_lit: "And if it is your wish to state It says: “And Aaron shall then offer his bull of sin-offering and atone for himself and his household. the bull has not yet been slaughtered.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.36b.12", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-036b-l43", kind: "gemara", he: "מַאי ״וְאִם נַפְשְׁךָ לוֹמַר״? וְכִי תֵּימָא נֵילַף מִשָּׂעִיר\nהַנַּעֲשֶׂה בִּפְנִים, שֶׁכַּפָּרָתוֹ בְּדָמִים, הֲרֵי\nהוּא אוֹמֵר ״וְכִפֶּר״, וַעֲדַיִין לֹא נִשְׁחַט הַפָּר.",
            vilna_line: 43, en: "The Gemara seeks to clarify the midrash: <b>What</b> is the meaning of: <b>And if it is your wish to say,</b> which indicates that there is room to undermine the first source? Why is a second source required? The Gemara answers: <b>And if you say</b> that instead of deriving the atonement of the bull from the atonement of the scapegoat, <b>let us derive</b> it <b>from the goat that is offered within, whose atonement is</b> achieved <b>through</b> sprinkling its <b>blood</b> in the innermost sanctum; therefore, it was taught in the <i>baraita</i> that <b>it says: And atone, and the bull has not yet been slaughtered.</b>", en_lit: "What And if it is your wish to say, And if you say let us derive from the goat that is offered within, whose atonement is through blood it says: And atone, and the bull has not yet been slaughtered.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.36b.13", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } }
        ],
