            vilna_line: 8, en: "The Gemara <b>raises an objection: One who recites <i>Shema</i></b> in the <b>morning with the men of the priestly watch,</b> who served in the Temple during a given week, <b>or with the men of the non-priestly watch,</b> designated groups of Israelites who accompanied the priestly watch to Jerusalem that week, <b>did not fulfill</b> his obligation. That is <b>because the men of the priestly watch</b> recite <i>Shema</i> too <b>early</b> so that they will have sufficient time to perform the Temple service, <b>and the men of the non-priestly watch,</b> who recite lengthy prayers and stand over the daily morning offering when it is sacrificed, <b>postpone</b> reciting <i>Shema</i>. For whom, then, did the emanating sparks signal the time to recite <i>Shema</i>? <b>Abaye said:</b> It was an indicator <b>for the rest of the people in Jerusalem,</b> who recited <i>Shema</i> at the appropriate time to recite <i>Shema</i>.", en_lit: "raises an objection: One who recites Shema morning with the men of the priestly watch, or with the men of the non-priestly watch, did not fulfill because the men of the priestly watch early and the men of the non-priestly watch, postpone Abaye said: for the rest of the people in Jerusalem,",
