          { id: "yoma-059a-l37", kind: "gemara", he: "תַּנְיָא, חֲנַנְיָא אוֹמֵר: בְּצַד צְפוֹנִי הוּא נוֹתֵן,\nרַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר: בְּצַד דְּרוֹמִי הוּא נוֹתֵן. בְּמַאי קָמִיפַּלְגִי? מָר סָבַר: פִּיתְחָא\nבְּדָרוֹם קָאֵי, וּמָר סָבַר: פִּיתְחָא בְּצָפוֹן קָאֵי.",
            vilna_line: 37, en: "§ <b>It was taught</b> in a <i>baraita</i> that <b>Ḥananya says:</b> The priest <b>presents</b> seven sprinklings <b>on the north side</b> of the altar, and <b>Rabbi Yosei says: He presents</b> them <b>on the south side.</b> The Gemara asks: <b>With regard to what</b> principle do <b>they disagree?</b> The Gemara explains: <b>One Sage,</b> Ḥananya, <b>holds</b> that <b>the entrance</b> was <b>positioned in the south,</b> and therefore the High Priest begins the sprinklings from that side. <b>And one Sage,</b> Rabbi Yosei, <b>holds</b> that <b>the entrance</b> was <b>positioned in the north,</b> and he therefore begins to sprinkle on the altar from the north side.", en_lit: "It was taught Ḥananya says: presents on the north side Rabbi Yosei says: He presents on the south side. With regard to what they disagree? One Sage, holds the entrance positioned in the south, And one Sage, holds the entrance positioned in the north,",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.59a.11", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-059a-l39", kind: "gemara", he: "דְּכוּלֵּי עָלְמָא מִיהָא, הֵיכָא דְּגָמְרָן מַתָּנוֹת\nדִּקְרָנוֹת, הָתָם יָהֵיב עַל גַּגּוֹ. מַאי טַעְמָא? אָמַר קְרָא: ״וְטִהֲרוֹ וְקִדְּשׁוֹ״ — מָקוֹם שֶׁקִּדְּשׁוֹ,\nשָׁם טִיהֲרוֹ.",
            vilna_line: 39, en: "The Gemara comments: <b>Everyone</b> agrees <b>in any case</b> that in the place <b>where he finishes the presentations</b> of the <b>corners, that</b> is <b>where he places</b> the blood <b>on</b> the altar’s <b>top.</b> They disagree only about the location of the final presentation, whether it is on the south or the north side. The Gemara asks: <b>What is the reason</b> for this agreement? The Gemara answers that <b>the verse states:</b> “And he shall sprinkle of the blood upon it with his finger seven times, <b>and cleanse it and sanctify it”</b> (Leviticus 16:19), which indicates that the <b>place he sanctified</b> by sprinkling blood, the corner of the altar where he sprinkled last, <b>there he shall</b> also begin to <b>cleanse</b> and sprinkle on top.", en_lit: "Everyone in any case where he finishes the presentations corners, that where he places on top. What is the reason the verse states: and cleanse it and sanctify it” place he sanctified there he shall cleanse",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.59a.12", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } }
