        lines: [
          { id: "yoma-061b-l22", kind: "gemara", he: "תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְלָקַח\nמִדַּם הָאָשָׁם״, יָכוֹל בִּכְלִי — תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר: ״וְנָתַן״. מָה נְתִינָה\nבְּעַצְמוֹ שֶׁל כֹּהֵן — אַף לְקִיחָה בְּעַצְמוֹ שֶׁל כֹּהֵן.",
            vilna_line: 22, en: "§ <b>The Sages taught:</b> “And the priest <b>shall take of the blood of the guilt-offering,</b> and the priest shall put it upon the tip of the right ear of him who is to be purified, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the big toe of his right foot” (Leviticus 14:14). One <b>might</b> have thought that he should take it <b>in a vessel;</b> therefore, <b>the verse states: “And put.” Just as putting</b> means <b>with the priest’s own</b> body, <b>so too, taking</b> means <b>with the priest’s own</b> body.", en_lit: "The Sages taught: shall take of the blood of the guilt-offering, might in a vessel; the verse states: “And put.” Just as putting with the priest’s own so too, taking with the priest’s own",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.61b.7", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-061b-l25", kind: "gemara", he: "יָכוֹל אַף לַמִּזְבֵּחַ כֵּן — תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר: ״כִּי כַּחַטָּאת הָאָשָׁם\nהוּא״. מָה חַטָּאת טְעוּנָה כְּלִי — אַף אָשָׁם טָעוּן\nכְּלִי. נִמְצֵאתָ אַתָּה אוֹמֵר: אֲשַׁם מְצוֹרָע שְׁנֵי\nכֹהֲנִים מְקַבְּלִים אֶת דָּמוֹ, אֶחָד בַּיָּד וְאֶחָד\nבִּכְלִי. זֶה שֶׁקִּבֵּל בִּכְלִי בָּא לוֹ אֵצֶל מִזְבֵּחַ,\nוְזֶה שֶׁקִּיבֵּל בַּיָּד בָּא לוֹ אֵצֶל מְצוֹרָע.",
            vilna_line: 25, en: "The <i>baraita</i> continues: One <b>might</b> have thought that <b>even</b> with regard to the blood of the leper’s guilt-offering that he presents <b>on the altar,</b> like the blood of other guilt-offerings, it is <b>so</b> that he collects the blood in his hand rather than with a vessel. Therefore, <b>the verse states: “For as the sin-offering is, so is the guilt-offering”</b> (Leviticus 14:13): <b>Just as a sin-offering requires a vessel</b> for collection of its blood, <b>so too,</b> the blood of <b>a guilt-offering requires</b> collection in <b>a vessel. And you find that you</b> must <b>say: The leper’s guilt-offering</b> requires <b>two priests</b> to <b>collect its blood; one</b> collects <b>by hand, and</b> the other <b>one</b> collects <b>in a vessel. The one who collected in a vessel comes to the altar</b> and sprinkles some of the blood on it, <b>and the one who collected by hand comes to the leper</b> and sprinkles some of the blood on him.", en_lit: "might even on the altar, so the verse states: “For as the sin-offering is, so is the guilt-offering” Just as a sin-offering requires a vessel so too, a guilt-offering requires a vessel. And you find that you say: The leper’s guilt-offering two priests collect its blood; one by hand, and one in a vessel. The one who collected in a vessel comes to the altar and the one who collected by hand comes to the leper",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.61b.8", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } }
        ],
