        lines: [
          { id: "yoma-070b-l01", kind: "gemara", he: "וְאַחַר כָּךְ שָׂעִיר הַנַּעֲשֶׂה בַּחוּץ, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״שְׂעִיר\nעִזִּים אֶחָד חַטָּאת מִלְּבַד חַטַּאת הַכִּפּוּרִים״,\nוְאַחַר כָּךְ אֵילוֹ וְאֵיל הָעָם, וְאַחַר כָּךְ אֵימוּרֵי חַטָּאת,\nוְאַחַר כָּךְ תָּמִיד שֶׁל בֵּין הָעַרְבַּיִם.",
            vilna_line: 1, en: "<b>And afterward, the goat whose</b> services <b>are performed outside</b> is sacrificed, <b>as it is stated: “One goat for a sin-offering besides the sin-offering of atonement</b> and the daily burnt-offering, and its meal-offering, and their libations” (Numbers 29:11), indicating that the goat sin-offering is sacrificed after the other offerings of the day. <b>And afterward</b> he offers <b>his ram and the ram of the people, and afterward</b> he places upon the altar the <b>portions of the sin-offering</b> to be consumed on the altar, <b>and afterward he sacrifices the daily afternoon offering.</b>", en_lit: "And afterward, the goat whose are performed outside as it is stated: “One goat for a sin-offering besides the sin-offering of atonement And afterward his ram and the ram of the people, and afterward portions of the sin-offering and afterward he sacrifices the daily afternoon offering.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.70b.1", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-070b-l04", kind: "gemara", he: "מַאי טַעְמָא\nדְּרַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר? עָבֵיד כְּדִכְתִיב: עָבֵיד בְּרֵישָׁא\nדְּתוֹרַת כֹּהֲנִים, וַהֲדַר עָבֵיד דְּחוֹמֶשׁ הַפְּקוּדִים.",
            vilna_line: 4, en: "<b>What is the reason</b> for the opinion <b>of Rabbi Eliezer?</b> The High Priest <b>acts in accordance with</b> the order in <b>which it is written</b> in the Torah: <b>First he performs</b> the services described in <b>Leviticus, and afterward he performs</b> the additional offerings mentioned in <b>the book of Numbers.</b>", en_lit: "What is the reason of Rabbi Eliezer? acts in accordance with which it is written First he performs Leviticus, and afterward he performs the book of Numbers.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.70b.2", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-070b-l07", kind: "gemara", he: "וְרַבִּי עֲקִיבָא? כִּדְקָתָנֵי טַעְמָא: ״מִלְּבַד עוֹלַת\nהַבֹּקֶר אֲשֶׁר לְעוֹלַת הַתָּמִיד״, אַלְמָא מוּסָפִין\nעִם תָּמִיד שֶׁל שַׁחַר עָבֵיד לְהוּ.",
            vilna_line: 7, en: "<b>And</b> what is <b>Rabbi Akiva’s</b> reasoning? His <b>reasoning</b> is <b>that as</b> the <i>Tosefta</i> <b>teaches</b> that the verse states: <b>“Besides the morning burnt-offering which is the daily burnt-offering</b> you shall sacrifice these” (Numbers 28:23), <b>it is apparent</b> that the sacrifice of the <b>additional offerings</b> should be <b>performed</b> together <b>with the daily morning offering.</b>", en_lit: "And Rabbi Akiva’s reasoning that as teaches “Besides the morning burnt-offering which is the daily burnt-offering it is apparent additional offerings performed with the daily morning offering.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.70b.3", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } },
          { id: "yoma-070b-l09", kind: "gemara", he: "וְרַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר,\nהַאי ״מִלְּבַד חַטַּאת הַכִּפּוּרִים״ מַאי עָבֵיד לֵיהּ?\nהַהוּא מִיבְּעֵי לֵיהּ, עַל מָה שֶׁזֶּה מְכַפֵּר — זֶה\nמְכַפֵּר.",
            vilna_line: 9, en: "The Gemara asks: <b>And Rabbi Eliezer, what does he do with this</b> verse: <b>“Besides the sin-offering of atonement,”</b> which was the basis for Rabbi Akiva’s opinion? <b>That</b> verse <b>is necessary for him</b> to derive from it that <b>for what this one,</b> the goat sin-offering whose blood is sprinkled inside the Holy of Holies, <b>atones, that one,</b> the goat sin-offering of the additional offerings whose services are performed in the Temple courtyard, also <b>atones.</b>", en_lit: "And Rabbi Eliezer, what does he do with this “Besides the sin-offering of atonement,” That is necessary for him for what this one, atones, that one, atones.",
            sefaria_ref: "Yoma.70b.4", commentaries: { rashi: [], tosafot: [] } }
        ],
