            speaker: "Gemara",
            text: "A baraita permits one traveling to greet his father, his teacher, or someone greater than him in wisdom to cross a river up to his neck, without concern for the Yom Kippur bathing prohibition, since the purpose is the mitzva of the visit rather than pleasure.",
