          coreMove: "The Gemara establishes the principle: the Torah was given to live by, not to die by. Every prohibition exists within a framework that values life. When life is threatened, the Torah itself authorizes - and even requires - its own override. Pikuach nefesh is not an exception to Torah but an expression of it.",
