            text: "The Mishnah says repentance atones for both positive and negative mitzvot. The Gemara objects: a negative mitzva is more severe (it carries lashes), so if repentance handles that, why state the lighter positive mitzva? Rav Yehuda reframes the Mishnah: repentance atones for a positive mitzva and for a negative mitzva that can be corrected by a positive act (lav hanitak la'aseh), which has the lenient status of a positive command.",
