            type: "case",
            label: "When the priestly blessing is said four times a day",
            speaker: "Mishnah (Ta'anit)",
            text: "A Mishnah in Ta'anit: three times a year the priests bless four times in one day - shacharit, musaf, mincha, and ne'ila. These three occasions are communal fasts for rain (which have ne'ila), non-priestly watches (ma'amadot), and Yom Kippur. This introduces ne'ila as a distinct prayer.",
